Eclipse 2018: This NASA GSFC map outlines the solar eclipse's reach on Saturday
During this global window of opportunity, the eclipse will be seen from parts of Scandinavia, Canada, Russia, China and South and North Korea. If you happen to find yourself on the North Pole on the morning of the eclipse, you will be best positioned to see about 65 percent of eclipse coverage. The NASA animation embedded below demonstrates how the Moon��s shadow cast by the Sun will behave on Saturday. The shadow will extend from the nightside of Earth over Canada and Greenland, before it brushes against the northernmost parts of Europe.
